#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:4
msgid "既約k点と結晶の対称性"
msgstr "Irreducible k-Points and Crystal Symmetry"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:6
msgid ""
"結晶の電子状態計算では、まずブリルアンゾーン（BZ）の多数のk点での計算を行い、最後にそれらの和をとって最終的な物理量を求める。 "
"結晶の対称性を使うと、同じ情報を持つ点をまとめ、代表点だけで計算できる。 本稿ではブロッホ関数の変換からその理由を導き、代表点の重みを説明する。"
msgstr ""
"In an electronic structure calculation for a crystal, we first calculate "
"at many k-points in the Brillouin zone (BZ), then sum their contributions"
" to obtain the physical quantities of interest. Crystal symmetry allows "
"us to group points that carry the same information and calculate only the"
" representatives. We derive why this works from the transformation of "
"Bloch functions and explain the weights of the representative points."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:10
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`ブロッホの定理<blochstheorem>`、 :ref:`ブリルアンゾーン<first-brillouin-"
"zone>`、:ref:`k点メッシュ<kpoint_sampling>`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: :ref:`Bloch’s Theorem <blochstheorem>`, the "
":ref:`Brillouin Zone <first-brillouin-zone>`, and :ref:`k-Point Meshes "
"<kpoint_sampling>`."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:13
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:15
msgid "結晶の対称操作が波数とエネルギーに及ぼす関係を導く。"
msgstr ""
"Derive how crystal symmetry operations transform wave vectors and relate "
"their energies."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:16
msgid "既約k点の重みが元のメッシュの和を再現することと、その条件を説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Explain how the weights of irreducible k-points reproduce the sum over "
"the original mesh and specify the conditions for this to work."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:19
msgid "結晶の対称操作"
msgstr "Crystal Symmetry Operations"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:21
msgid ""
":ref:`結晶の対称操作<crystal-symmetry-operations>`\\ の線形部分を :math:`Q`、 並進部分を "
":math:`\\boldsymbol t` とする。まとめて"
msgstr ""
"For a :ref:`crystal symmetry operation <crystal-symmetry-operations>`\\ ,"
" let :math:`Q` be the linear part and :math:`\\boldsymbol t` the "
"translational part. We write the operation as"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:24
#, python-brace-format
msgid "g=\\{Q\\mid\\boldsymbol t\\}"
msgstr "g=\\{Q\\mid\\boldsymbol t\\}"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:29
msgid ""
"と表すことにする。位置 :math:`\\boldsymbol r` にこれを作用させると、位置 :math:`\\boldsymbol r'` "
"に移るという場合"
msgstr ""
"When the operation takes position :math:`\\boldsymbol r` to position "
":math:`\\boldsymbol r'`, the forward and inverse transformations are"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:31
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\boldsymbol r' = g\\boldsymbol r=Q\\boldsymbol r+\\boldsymbol t,\\qquad\n"
"g^{-1}\\boldsymbol r' = \\boldsymbol r = Q^{-1}(\\boldsymbol "
"r'-\\boldsymbol t)"
msgstr ""
"\\boldsymbol r' = g\\boldsymbol r=Q\\boldsymbol r+\\boldsymbol t,\\qquad\n"
"g^{-1}\\boldsymbol r' = \\boldsymbol r = Q^{-1}(\\boldsymbol "
"r'-\\boldsymbol t)"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:37
msgid ""
"となる。Cartesian座標で :math:`Q` は直交行列、 :math:`\\boldsymbol t` はベクトルである。 "
"この直交部分の集まりが\\ :ref:`結晶の点群<crystal-point-group>`\\ である。以下では、原子配置だけでなく、 "
"電子のハミルトニアンも不変に保つ操作を考える。"
msgstr ""
"In Cartesian coordinates, :math:`Q` is an orthogonal matrix and "
":math:`\\boldsymbol t` is a vector. The set of these orthogonal parts is "
"the \\ :ref:`crystal point group <crystal-point-group>`\\ . Below, we "
"consider operations that leave both the atomic arrangement and the "
"electronic Hamiltonian invariant."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:42
msgid "ブロッホ関数の変換"
msgstr "Transformation of Bloch Functions"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:44
msgid ""
"スピンを明示しないスカラー波動関数を考える。波数 :math:`\\boldsymbol k` の ブロッホ関数は任意の格子並進 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol L` に対して"
msgstr ""
"Consider a scalar wave function without explicit spin. A Bloch function "
"of wave vector :math:`\\boldsymbol k` satisfies the following relation "
"for any lattice translation :math:`\\boldsymbol L`:"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:47
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}(\\boldsymbol r+\\boldsymbol L)\n"
"=e^{i\\boldsymbol k\\cdot\\boldsymbol L}\\psi_{\\boldsymbol "
"k}(\\boldsymbol r)"
msgstr ""
"\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}(\\boldsymbol r+\\boldsymbol L)\n"
"=e^{i\\boldsymbol k\\cdot\\boldsymbol L}\\psi_{\\boldsymbol "
"k}(\\boldsymbol r)"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:53
msgid "を満たす。 :eq:`ikp-operation` に対応する関数の変換を考える。関数と位置を同時に変換すると、それは元と何も変わらないので、"
msgstr ""
"Consider the transformation of the function corresponding to Equation :eq"
":`ikp-operation`. When both the function and the position are "
"transformed, the value stays the same:"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:55
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})(g\\boldsymbol r)\n"
"=\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}(\\boldsymbol r)"
msgstr ""
"(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})(g\\boldsymbol r)\n"
"=\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}(\\boldsymbol r)"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:61
msgid "となる（\\ :math:`U_g` は変換に対応した演算子とする）。ここから"
msgstr ""
"Here \\ :math:`U_g` is the operator corresponding to the transformation. "
"It follows that"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:63
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})(\\boldsymbol r)\n"
"=\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}(g^{-1}\\boldsymbol r)\n"
"=\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}\\!\\left(Q^{-1}(\\boldsymbol r-\\boldsymbol "
"t)\\right)"
msgstr ""
"(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})(\\boldsymbol r)\n"
"=\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}(g^{-1}\\boldsymbol r)\n"
"=\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}\\!\\left(Q^{-1}(\\boldsymbol r-\\boldsymbol "
"t)\\right)"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:70
msgid "が導かれ、これで演算子 :math:`U_g` の作用が具体的に書き下せた事になる。"
msgstr "This gives the explicit action of :math:`U_g`."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:77
msgid "|symmetry-kpoint-mapping|"
msgstr "Transformation of Wave Vectors Under Symmetry Operations"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:79
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`g` で移した結晶は元の結晶と同じなので、格子並進も格子並進に移り、 :math:`Q\\boldsymbol L` と "
":math:`Q^{-1}\\boldsymbol L` も格子並進である。 :eq:`ikp-bloch` を "
":math:`Q^{-1}\\boldsymbol L` に使い、 :math:`Q` の直交性 "
"（:math:`Q^{-1}=Q^{\\mathsf T}`\\ ）から :math:`\\boldsymbol k\\cdot "
"Q^{-1}\\boldsymbol L=(Q\\boldsymbol k)\\cdot\\boldsymbol L` とすると"
msgstr ""
"Applying :math:`g` leaves the crystal unchanged, so lattice translations "
"map to lattice translations. In particular, :math:`Q\\boldsymbol L` and "
":math:`Q^{-1}\\boldsymbol L` are lattice translations. Applying Equation "
":eq:`ikp-bloch` to :math:`Q^{-1}\\boldsymbol L` and using the "
"orthogonality of :math:`Q` (:math:`Q^{-1}=Q^{\\mathsf T}`\\ ), so that "
":math:`\\boldsymbol k\\cdot Q^{-1}\\boldsymbol L=(Q\\boldsymbol "
"k)\\cdot\\boldsymbol L`, gives"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:85
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})(\\boldsymbol r+\\boldsymbol L)\n"
"&=\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}\\!\\left(Q^{-1}(\\boldsymbol r-\\boldsymbol "
"t)+Q^{-1}\\boldsymbol L\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=e^{i\\boldsymbol k\\cdot Q^{-1}\\boldsymbol L}(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol "
"k})(\\boldsymbol r)\\\\\n"
"&=e^{i(Q\\boldsymbol k)\\cdot\\boldsymbol L}(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol "
"k})(\\boldsymbol r).\n"
"\\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})(\\boldsymbol r+\\boldsymbol L)\n"
"&=\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}\\!\\left(Q^{-1}(\\boldsymbol r-\\boldsymbol "
"t)+Q^{-1}\\boldsymbol L\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=e^{i\\boldsymbol k\\cdot Q^{-1}\\boldsymbol L}(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol "
"k})(\\boldsymbol r)\\\\\n"
"&=e^{i(Q\\boldsymbol k)\\cdot\\boldsymbol L}(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol "
"k})(\\boldsymbol r).\n"
"\\end{aligned}"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:95
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"したがって :math:`U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}` は波数 :math:`Q\\boldsymbol k` "
"のブロッホ条件を満たす。 逆格子ベクトル :math:`\\boldsymbol G` に対して :math:`e^{i\\boldsymbol "
"G\\cdot\\boldsymbol L}=1` なので、 :math:`\\boldsymbol G` "
"だけ違う波数は同じブロッホ条件を与える。変換後の波数を :math:`\\boldsymbol k'` と書けば"
msgstr ""
"Thus :math:`U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}` satisfies the Bloch condition for "
"wave vector :math:`Q\\boldsymbol k`. For a reciprocal lattice vector "
":math:`\\boldsymbol G`, we have :math:`e^{i\\boldsymbol "
"G\\cdot\\boldsymbol L}=1`, so wave vectors that differ by "
":math:`\\boldsymbol G` give the same Bloch condition. If we write the "
"transformed wave vector as :math:`\\boldsymbol k'`, it satisfies"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:100
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\boldsymbol k'\\equiv Q\\boldsymbol k\\pmod{\\boldsymbol G}"
msgstr "\\boldsymbol k'\\equiv Q\\boldsymbol k\\pmod{\\boldsymbol G}"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:105
msgid "である。並進部分 :math:`\\boldsymbol t` は波数の行先には現れないが、波動関数の形や位相には影響する。"
msgstr ""
"The translational part :math:`\\boldsymbol t` does not enter the mapping "
"of wave vectors, but it affects the shape and phase of the wave function."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:107
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`Q` はCartesian座標の行列である。\\ :ref:`格子行列<lattice-translations>` "
":math:`A` と\\ :ref:`逆格子行列<reciprocal-lattice>` :math:`B=2\\pi "
"A^{-\\mathsf T}` を使い、実格子の\\ :ref:`分率座標<coordinates>`\\ で同じ操作を "
":math:`W=A^{-1}QA` と表すと、逆格子の分率座標では :math:`B^{-1}QB=A^{\\mathsf "
"T}QA^{-\\mathsf T}=(W^{-1})^{\\mathsf T}` となる。最後の等号には :math:`Q^{-\\mathsf"
" T}=Q` を使った。一般には :math:`W` をそのままk点の分率座標に掛けられない。"
msgstr ""
"The matrix :math:`Q` is expressed in Cartesian coordinates. Let \\ "
":ref:`lattice matrix <lattice-translations>` :math:`A` and \\ "
":ref:`reciprocal lattice matrix <reciprocal-lattice>` :math:`B=2\\pi "
"A^{-\\mathsf T}` describe the two lattices. If the same operation in "
"real-space \\ :ref:`fractional coordinates <coordinates>`\\  is "
":math:`W=A^{-1}QA`, its matrix in reciprocal-space fractional coordinates"
" is :math:`B^{-1}QB=A^{\\mathsf T}QA^{-\\mathsf T}=(W^{-1})^{\\mathsf "
"T}`. The last equality uses :math:`Q^{-\\mathsf T}=Q`. In general, we "
"cannot apply :math:`W` directly to the fractional coordinates of a "
"k-point."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:114
msgid "エネルギーの等価性"
msgstr "Equality of Energies at Equivalent k-Points"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:116
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"ハミルトニアン :math:`H` がこの操作を保つとき、 :math:`HU_g=U_gH` である。 "
":math:`H\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}=\\varepsilon\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}` なら"
msgstr ""
"When this operation leaves the Hamiltonian :math:`H` invariant, "
":math:`HU_g=U_gH`. If :math:`H\\psi_{\\boldsymbol "
"k}=\\varepsilon\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}`, then"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:119
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"H(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})=U_gH\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}\n"
"=\\varepsilon(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})"
msgstr ""
"H(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})=U_gH\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}\n"
"=\\varepsilon(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:125
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"なので、 :math:`U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}` は :math:`Q\\boldsymbol k` "
"の同じエネルギーの固有状態である。 :math:`U_g` は1次独立な状態を1次独立な状態に移し、逆操作 :math:`g^{-1}` "
"で戻せるので、 :math:`\\boldsymbol k` と :math:`Q\\boldsymbol k` "
"のエネルギー固有値の集合は縮退度を含めて等しい。 各k点でバンドをエネルギーの低い順に番号付けると"
msgstr ""
"Thus :math:`U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}` is an eigenstate at "
":math:`Q\\boldsymbol k` with the same energy. The operator :math:`U_g` "
"maps linearly independent states to linearly independent states and can "
"be undone by the inverse operation :math:`g^{-1}`. Therefore, the sets of"
" energy eigenvalues at :math:`\\boldsymbol k` and :math:`Q\\boldsymbol k`"
" are identical, including their degeneracies. Numbering the bands at each"
" k-point in order of increasing energy gives"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:130
msgid ""
"\\varepsilon_n(Q\\boldsymbol k)=\\varepsilon_n(\\boldsymbol "
"k)\\qquad(n=1,2,\\ldots)"
msgstr ""
"\\varepsilon_n(Q\\boldsymbol k)=\\varepsilon_n(\\boldsymbol "
"k)\\qquad(n=1,2,\\ldots)"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:135
msgid ""
"である。ただし、変換後の状態が、 :math:`Q\\boldsymbol k` であらかじめ選んだ固有関数と "
"等しいとは限らない。位相は任意であり、縮退があると同じエネルギーの状態どうしが混ざり得る。"
msgstr ""
"However, the transformed state need not coincide with an eigenfunction "
"chosen in advance at :math:`Q\\boldsymbol k`. Its phase is arbitrary, and"
" states of the same energy can mix when there is degeneracy."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:141
msgid "等価なk点の組と代表点"
msgstr "Equivalent k-Points and Representative Points"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:143
msgid ""
"メッシュを自分自身に写す対称操作で、 :eq:`ikp-kmap` によって互いに移り合う点を一組にする。 行先は "
":math:`\\boldsymbol G` を法として考えるので、BZの境界で逆格子ベクトルだけ違う点は1点と数える。 "
"各組から1点ずつ選んだ代表が既約k点である。"
msgstr ""
"Use symmetry operations that map the mesh onto itself to group points "
"related by Equation :eq:`ikp-kmap`. Since the image is taken modulo "
":math:`\\boldsymbol G`, points on the BZ boundary that differ by a "
"reciprocal lattice vector count as one point. The irreducible k-points "
"are the representatives chosen one from each group."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:147
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"組の点数 :math:`m_i` は、使う操作の数 :math:`N_{\\rm op}` から決まる。代表点 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol k_i` を （:math:`\\boldsymbol G` を法として）自分自身に戻す操作が "
":math:`s_i` 個あるとする。 :math:`Q\\boldsymbol k_i\\equiv Q'\\boldsymbol k_i` "
"となるのは :math:`Q^{-1}Q'` が :math:`\\boldsymbol k_i` を戻すときなので、組のどの点にもちょうど "
":math:`s_i` 個の操作が行き着き、"
msgstr ""
"The number of points :math:`m_i` in a group follows from the number of "
"operations used, :math:`N_{\\rm op}`. Suppose the representative "
":math:`\\boldsymbol k_i` is mapped to itself modulo :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"G` by :math:`s_i` operations. The relation :math:`Q\\boldsymbol "
"k_i\\equiv Q'\\boldsymbol k_i` holds exactly when :math:`Q^{-1}Q'` maps "
":math:`\\boldsymbol k_i` to itself. Thus exactly :math:`s_i` operations "
"reach each point in the group, and"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:152
msgid "m_i=\\frac{N_{\\rm op}}{s_i}"
msgstr "m_i=\\frac{N_{\\rm op}}{s_i}"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:157
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"である。一般の点では :math:`s_i=1` で組は :math:`N_{\\rm op}` 点になり、Γ点のような対称性の高い点では "
"組が小さい。"
msgstr ""
"At a general point, :math:`s_i=1` and the group contains :math:`N_{\\rm "
"op}` points. At a high-symmetry point such as the Γ point, the group is "
"smaller."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:163
msgid "|irreducible-kpoint-weights|"
msgstr "Weights of Irreducible k-Points and Integration"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:165
msgid "等間隔メッシュの和を、既約k点 :math:`\\boldsymbol k_i` だけの重み付きの和で置き換える。"
msgstr ""
"We replace the sum over the uniform mesh with a weighted sum over only "
"the irreducible k-points :math:`\\boldsymbol k_i`:"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:167
msgid ""
"\\frac{1}{N_k}\\sum_{\\boldsymbol k\\in\\text{メッシュ}}A(\\boldsymbol "
"k)=\\sum_i w_i\\,A(\\boldsymbol k_i),\n"
"\\qquad\\sum_i w_i=1"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{1}{N_k}\\sum_{\\boldsymbol k\\in\\text{mesh}}A(\\boldsymbol "
"k)=\\sum_i w_i\\,A(\\boldsymbol k_i),\n"
"\\qquad\\sum_i w_i=1"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:173
msgid ""
":math:`N_k=n_1n_2n_3` はメッシュの点の数である。全 :math:`N_k` 点が等しい重みを持ち、被積分量 "
":math:`A(\\boldsymbol k)` が同じ組で等しいとき、重みは :math:`w_i=m_i/N_k` になり、"
msgstr ""
"Here :math:`N_k=n_1n_2n_3` is the number of mesh points. When all "
":math:`N_k` points have equal weight and the integrand "
":math:`A(\\boldsymbol k)` is constant within each group, the weights are "
":math:`w_i=m_i/N_k`, giving"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:176
msgid ""
"\\frac{1}{N_k}\\sum_{\\boldsymbol k\\in\\text{メッシュ}}A(\\boldsymbol k)\n"
"=\\sum_{i=1}^{N_{\\rm irr}}\\frac{m_i}{N_k}A(\\boldsymbol k_i),\\qquad\n"
"\\sum_i m_i=N_k,\\quad \\sum_i\\frac{m_i}{N_k}=1"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{1}{N_k}\\sum_{\\boldsymbol k\\in\\text{mesh}}A(\\boldsymbol k)\n"
"=\\sum_{i=1}^{N_{\\rm irr}}\\frac{m_i}{N_k}A(\\boldsymbol k_i),\\qquad\n"
"\\sum_i m_i=N_k,\\quad \\sum_i\\frac{m_i}{N_k}=1"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:183
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"と書ける。代表点に組の点数を掛けることで、元の和を正確に再現する。 :math:`A(\\boldsymbol k)` "
"がエネルギーと占有数だけで決まる量（バンドエネルギーや電子数）なら、 :eq:`ikp-bands` "
"から同じ組で等しい。一方、電子密度へのk点ごとの寄与は位置の関数で、 :eq:`ikp-transform` から "
":math:`|(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})(\\boldsymbol "
"r)|^2=|\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}(g^{-1}\\boldsymbol r)|^2` なので、 "
":math:`Q\\boldsymbol k` の寄与は :math:`\\boldsymbol k` の寄与を :math:`g` "
"で移したものになる。 代表点だけの和を、各操作で移して平均（対称化）してから使う。"
msgstr ""
"Multiplying the value at each representative by the number of points in "
"its group exactly reproduces the original sum. If :math:`A(\\boldsymbol "
"k)` depends only on energies and occupation numbers, as do the band "
"energy and electron count, Equation :eq:`ikp-bands` shows that its value "
"is the same throughout each group. By contrast, the contribution of each "
"k-point to the electron density is a function of position. Equation :eq"
":`ikp-transform` gives :math:`|(U_g\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k})(\\boldsymbol "
"r)|^2=|\\psi_{\\boldsymbol k}(g^{-1}\\boldsymbol r)|^2`, so the "
"contribution at :math:`Q\\boldsymbol k` is the contribution at "
":math:`\\boldsymbol k` transformed by :math:`g`. The sum over "
"representatives alone is used after symmetrization, by transforming it "
"under each operation and averaging the results."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:191
msgid "正方格子の2次元メッシュ"
msgstr "Two-Dimensional Mesh on a Square Lattice"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:193
msgid ""
"90度回転と鏡映の8操作を持つ正方格子の結晶で、Γ点を中心とする :math:`3\\times3` メッシュを考える。 逆格子の基本ベクトルを "
":math:`\\boldsymbol b_1,\\boldsymbol b_2` とすると、 :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"k=s_1\\boldsymbol b_1+s_2\\boldsymbol b_2` の :math:`s_1,s_2` はそれぞれ "
":math:`-1/3,0,1/3` のいずれかである。:numref:`fig-irreducible-square-mesh`\\ "
"では、9点が 中心、軸上、対角方向の3組に分かれる。回転や鏡映で行き来できる点は同じ記号で示す。"
msgstr ""
"Consider a Γ-point-centered :math:`3\\times3` mesh for a square-lattice "
"crystal with eight symmetry operations generated by 90-degree rotation "
"and reflection. Let :math:`\\boldsymbol b_1,\\boldsymbol b_2` be the "
"primitive reciprocal lattice vectors. In :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"k=s_1\\boldsymbol b_1+s_2\\boldsymbol b_2`, each of :math:`s_1,s_2` is "
"one of :math:`-1/3,0,1/3`. In :numref:`fig-irreducible-square-mesh`\\ , "
"the nine points fall into three groups: the center, points on the axes, "
"and points along the diagonals. Points related by rotation or reflection "
"have the same marker."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:199
msgid "第1ブリルアンゾーンの正方形を薄青、既約な三角形の領域を薄緑で示す。中心、軸上、対角の各組から1点ずつを輪で囲み、重み1/9、4/9、4/9を添える。"
msgstr ""
"The square of the first Brillouin zone is light blue, and the irreducible"
" triangular region is light green. One point from each group (center, on "
"axes, on diagonals) is circled. Their respective weights are 1/9, 4/9, "
"and 4/9."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:205
msgid ""
"横軸と縦軸は逆格子の分率座標。薄青の正方形は第1ブリルアンゾーン （:math:`-1/2\\le "
"s_i<1/2`）、薄緑の三角形は既約な領域の一例 （:math:`0\\le s_2\\le "
"s_1<1/2`）である。輪で囲んだ3点が各組の代表点で、 右にそれぞれの正規化した重みを示す。"
msgstr ""
"The horizontal and vertical axes give fractional coordinates in the "
"reciprocal lattice. The light blue square is the first Brillouin zone "
"(:math:`-1/2\\le s_i<1/2`), and the light green triangle is an example of"
" an irreducible region (:math:`0\\le s_2\\le s_1<1/2`). The three circled"
" points are the group representatives. Their normalized weights appear on"
" the right."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:210
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Iは中心のΓ点、IIは軸上、IIIは対角方向の点である。Γ点は8操作すべてで自分自身に戻るので :math:`m=8/8=1`\\ "
"、軸上の点はその軸に沿う鏡映と恒等操作の2個で戻るので :math:`m=8/2=4`\\ 、 対角方向の点も対角線に沿う鏡映と恒等操作で戻るので"
" :math:`m=4` である。 :eq:`ikp-weight` の重みはそれぞれ :math:`1/9,4/9,4/9` となり、 "
"例えば各組での値を :math:`A_{\\rm I},A_{\\rm II},A_{\\rm III}` とすると、元の9点の平均は "
":math:`(A_{\\rm I}+4A_{\\rm II}+4A_{\\rm III})/9` である。鏡映の線に乗らない一般の点があれば、 "
"その組は8点になる。"
msgstr ""
"Group I is the central Γ point, II the points on the axes, and III those "
"along the diagonals. All eight operations map Γ back to itself, so "
":math:`m=8/8=1`\\ . Reflection across the axis and the identity map a "
"point on an axis back to itself, so :math:`m=8/2=4`\\ . Likewise, "
"reflection across a diagonal and the identity map a point on a diagonal "
"back to itself, so :math:`m=4`. The weights in Equation :eq:`ikp-weight` "
"are :math:`1/9,4/9,4/9`, respectively. For example, if the values in the "
"three groups are :math:`A_{\\rm I},A_{\\rm II},A_{\\rm III}`, the "
"original nine-point average is :math:`(A_{\\rm I}+4A_{\\rm II}+4A_{\\rm "
"III})/9`. A general point off the reflection lines would belong to a "
"group of eight points."

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:219
msgid "Cuの計算例"
msgstr "Calculation Example for Cu"

#: ../../solid/irreducible_kpoints.rst:221
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`Quloud ExamplesのCuの計算 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/kpoints/kpoint_convergence.html#sec-kp-irreducible>`_"
" では、fcc Cuの基本単位胞についてΓ点を含む :math:`4\\times4\\times4` メッシュの 64点が、Quantum "
"ESPRESSO 7.5で8個の既約k点にまとめられる。各点の座標と重みはリンク先の表にある。 fccの点群の操作は :math:`N_{\\rm"
" op}=48` 個である。各組の点数 :math:`m_i` は、 代表点を自分自身に戻す操作の数 :math:`s_i` "
"で48を割ると得られる（式 :eq:`ikp-orbit`）。"
msgstr ""
"In the Cu section of the Quloud calculation example “`How Many k-Points "
"Are Needed? Convergence for Metallic Cu and Semiconducting Si "
"<https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/kpoints/kpoint_convergence.html#sec-kp-"
"irreducible>`_,” Quantum ESPRESSO 7.5 reduces the 64 points of a "
":math:`4\\times4\\times4` mesh that includes the Γ point for the "
"primitive cell of fcc Cu to eight irreducible k-points. The linked table "
"gives the coordinates and weights of the irreducible k-points. The fcc "
"point group has :math:`N_{\\rm op}=48` operations. The number of points "
":math:`m_i` in each group is 48 divided by the number of operations "
":math:`s_i` that map its representative back to itself (Equation :eq"
":`ikp-orbit`)."

